    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1405">

                <pb facs="1750" n="1550" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1550"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Potsdam/8–745: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1405<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent—niact</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-08-07T22:00:00+02:00">August 7, 1945—10
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4769. Bidault requested Bogomolov, Duff
                        Cooper and myself to call this evening. He delivered to us six
                    identical notes containing the views of the French Govt on the decisions made at
                    Potsdam. The French Govt accepts in each case the decisions but formulates
                    various <pb facs="1751" n="1551" xml:id="pg1551"/> “reservations”, “regrets” and
                    “observations”. (My 4722, Aug 6, 4 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1405-f1"/>)</p>
                <p>The texts of these six notes are being cabled in my six immediately following
                    telegrams.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
